-          "quote": "Input $f,g$, a constant grid $t_n=t_0+nh$ with $h>0$ and $N_t\\in\\mathbb N$, an initial pair $(X_0,Z_0)$, and a selected open tube inside the local branch chart of [[thm-index-one-dae-implicit-function-reduction]], where $g(t,x,z)=0$ is equivalent to $z=\\psi(t,x)$. Also input positive residual tolerances $\\eta_d,\\eta_a$, a finite Newton-correction budget $B\\in\\mathbb N_0$, and an initial algebraic-residual bound $\\eta_{a,0}\\ge0$. Return invalid-grid if $h\\le0$ or $N_t=0$, invalid-input for incompatible dimensions or data outside the function domains, and inconsistent-initial-data if $\\|g(t_0,X_0,Z_0)\\|_2>\\eta_{a,0}$.\n\nFor $n=1,\\ldots,N_t$, form the coupled update residual\n\n$$\nR_n(X,Z)=\\bigl(X-X_{n-1}-h f(t_n,X,Z),\\ g(t_n,X,Z)\\bigr)\n$$\n\nand the scaled square residual\n\n$$\n\\mathcal R_n(X,Z)=\\left(\\frac{X-X_{n-1}-h f(t_n,X,Z)}{h\\eta_d},\\ \\frac{g(t_n,X,Z)}{\\eta_a}\\right).\n$$\n\nUse $(X_{n-1},Z_{n-1})$ as the Newton seed, and call [[alg-finite-budget-newton-for-vector-residuals]] on $\\mathcal R_n$ with residual tolerance $1$, budget $B$, and the selected tube as its evaluation domain. If the returned status is root and the candidate lies in the selected tube, reevaluate $R_n$ once to retain both unscaled residuals, then append the candidate. Otherwise return the corresponding singular-Jacobian, invalid-trial, or iteration-budget-exhausted status and the already computed prefix. The input functions are defined on the selected tube, so no separate evaluation-failure branch is needed. If every step is accepted, return completed and the state sequence.\n\nAn accepted step satisfies $\\|r^d_n\\|_2\\le\\eta_d$ for the derivative residual $r^d_n=(X_n-X_{n-1})/h-f(t_n,X_n,Z_n)$, and $\\|r^a_n\\|_2\\le\\eta_a$ for the algebraic residual $r^a_n=g(t_n,X_n,Z_n)$. This follows because each block norm is at most the norm of their concatenation. root means only that the scaled residual tolerance was met; it does not assert an exact zero, uniqueness, Newton convergence from an arbitrary seed, or a discretization error bound.\n\nEach step solves a coupled block system with $d+m$ unknowns. At most $B$ Newton corrections and $B+1$ Newton residual evaluations are made per attempted step, plus at most one residual reevaluation to record the unscaled blocks after a root status. Each correction uses one solve with the current $(d+m)$-dimensional block Jacobian. Work per residual, Jacobian assembly, and linear solve depends on the backend.",
+          "quote": "Input $f,g$, a constant grid $t_n=t_0+nh$ with $h>0$ and $N_t\\in\\mathbb N$, an initial pair $(X_0,Z_0)$, and a selected open tube $\\mathcal T\\subset\\Omega$ inside the local branch chart of [[thm-index-one-dae-implicit-function-reduction]], where $g(t,x,z)=0$ is equivalent to $z=\\psi(t,x)$. For each time $t$, write $\\mathcal T_t=\\{(X,Z):(t,X,Z)\\in\\mathcal T\\}$ for the open state slice used as the Newton evaluation domain. Also input positive residual tolerances $\\eta_d,\\eta_a$, a finite Newton-correction budget $B\\in\\mathbb N_0$, and an initial algebraic-residual bound $\\eta_{a,0}\\ge0$. Return invalid-grid if $h\\le0$ or $N_t=0$, and invalid-input for incompatible dimensions, data outside the function domains, or $(X_0,Z_0)\\notin\\mathcal T_{t_0}$. Compute the starting algebraic residual once; return inconsistent-initial-data if $\\|g(t_0,X_0,Z_0)\\|_2>\\eta_{a,0}$.\n\nFor $n=1,\\ldots,N_t$, form the coupled update residual\n\n$$\nR_n(X,Z)=\\bigl(X-X_{n-1}-h f(t_n,X,Z),\\ g(t_n,X,Z)\\bigr)\n$$\n\nand the scaled square residual\n\n$$\n\\mathcal R_n(X,Z)=\\left(\\frac{X-X_{n-1}-h f(t_n,X,Z)}{h\\eta_d},\\ \\frac{g(t_n,X,Z)}{\\eta_a}\\right).\n$$\n\nUse $(X_{n-1},Z_{n-1})$ as the Newton seed. Before calling Newton, if $(X_{n-1},Z_{n-1})\\notin\\mathcal T_{t_n}$, return invalid-trial with the already computed prefix. Otherwise call [[alg-finite-budget-newton-for-vector-residuals]] on $\\mathcal R_n$ with residual tolerance $1$, budget $B$, and $\\mathcal T_{t_n}$ as its evaluation domain. If the returned status is root and the candidate lies in $\\mathcal T_{t_n}$, reevaluate $R_n$ once to retain both unscaled residuals, then append the candidate. Otherwise return the corresponding singular-Jacobian, invalid-trial, or iteration-budget-exhausted status and the already computed prefix. The input functions are defined on the selected tube, so no separate evaluation-failure branch is needed. If every step is accepted, return completed and the state sequence.\n\nAn accepted step satisfies $\\|r^d_n\\|_2\\le\\eta_d$ for the derivative residual $r^d_n=(X_n-X_{n-1})/h-f(t_n,X_n,Z_n)$, and $\\|r^a_n\\|_2\\le\\eta_a$ for the algebraic residual $r^a_n=g(t_n,X_n,Z_n)$. This follows because each block norm is at most the norm of their concatenation. root means only that the scaled residual tolerance was met; it does not assert an exact zero, uniqueness, Newton convergence from an arbitrary seed, or a discretization error bound.\n\nEach step solves a coupled block system with $d+m$ unknowns. At most $B$ Newton corrections and $B+1$ Newton residual evaluations are made per attempted step, plus at most one residual reevaluation to record the unscaled blocks after a root status. Each correction uses one solve with the current $(d+m)$-dimensional block Jacobian. Work per residual, Jacobian assembly, and linear solve depends on the backend.",
