-          "quote": "Input $f,g$, a constant grid $t_n=t_0+nh$ with $h>0$ and $N_t\\ge2$, two starting pairs $(X_0,Z_0),(X_1,Z_1)$, and a selected open tube inside the local branch chart of [[thm-index-one-dae-implicit-function-reduction]], where $g(t,x,z)=0$ is equivalent to $z=\\psi(t,x)$. Also input positive residual tolerances $\\eta_d,\\eta_a$ and a finite Newton-correction budget $B\\in\\mathbb N_0$. Each starting algebraic residual must meet its supplied bound; otherwise return inconsistent-initial-data. Return invalid-grid for a nonpositive step or fewer than two starting states, and invalid-input for incompatible dimensions or data outside the function domains.\n\nFor $n=2,\\ldots,N_t$, form\n\n$$\nR_n(X,Z)=\\bigl(3X-4X_{n-1}+X_{n-2}-2h f(t_n,X,Z),\\ g(t_n,X,Z)\\bigr)\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\mathcal R_n(X,Z)=\\left(\\frac{3X-4X_{n-1}+X_{n-2}-2h f(t_n,X,Z)}{2h\\eta_d},\\ \\frac{g(t_n,X,Z)}{\\eta_a}\\right).\n$$\n\nUse $(2X_{n-1}-X_{n-2},Z_{n-1})$ as the Newton seed and call [[alg-finite-budget-newton-for-vector-residuals]] on $\\mathcal R_n$ with tolerance $1$, budget $B$, and the selected tube as the evaluation domain. Append a candidate only when Newton reports root and the candidate lies in the tube; reevaluate $R_n$ once to record its unscaled residual blocks. Otherwise return the corresponding singular-Jacobian, invalid-trial, or iteration-budget-exhausted status with the computed prefix. The input functions are defined on the selected tube, so no separate evaluation-failure branch is needed. If all steps are accepted, return completed.\n\nFor an accepted step, the constant-step BDF2 derivative residual is\n$$\nr^d_n=\\frac{3X_n-4X_{n-1}+X_{n-2}}{2h}-f(t_n,X_n,Z_n),\n$$\nand the algebraic residual is $r^a_n=g(t_n,X_n,Z_n)$. The scaling ensures $\\|r^d_n\\|_2\\le\\eta_d$ and $\\|r^a_n\\|_2\\le\\eta_a$. The procedure makes no claim that Newton finds a root or that an accepted state is the exact selected branch root.\n\nEach step solves a coupled block system with $d+m$ unknowns. At most $B$ Newton corrections and $B+1$ Newton residual evaluations are made per attempted step, plus at most one residual reevaluation to record the unscaled blocks after a root status. Each correction uses one solve with the current $(d+m)$-dimensional block Jacobian. Work per residual, Jacobian assembly, and linear solve depends on the backend.",
+          "quote": "Input $f,g$, a constant grid $t_n=t_0+nh$ with $h>0$ and $N_t\\ge2$, two starting pairs $(X_0,Z_0),(X_1,Z_1)$, and a selected open tube $\\mathcal T\\subset\\Omega$ inside the local branch chart of [[thm-index-one-dae-implicit-function-reduction]], where $g(t,x,z)=0$ is equivalent to $z=\\psi(t,x)$. For each time $t$, write $\\mathcal T_t=\\{(X,Z):(t,X,Z)\\in\\mathcal T\\}$ for the open state slice used as the Newton evaluation domain. Also input positive residual tolerances $\\eta_d,\\eta_a$, a finite Newton-correction budget $B\\in\\mathbb N_0$, and two starting algebraic-residual bounds $\\eta_{a,0},\\eta_{a,1}\\ge0$. Return invalid-grid for a nonpositive step or fewer than two starting states, and invalid-input for incompatible dimensions, data outside the function domains, or $(X_j,Z_j)\\notin\\mathcal T_{t_j}$ for either $j=0,1$. Compute $r^a_j=g(t_j,X_j,Z_j)$ for both $j=0,1$; if $\\|r^a_j\\|_2>\\eta_{a,j}$ for either start, return inconsistent-initial-data.\n\nFor $n=2,\\ldots,N_t$, form\n\n$$\nR_n(X,Z)=\\bigl(3X-4X_{n-1}+X_{n-2}-2h f(t_n,X,Z),\\ g(t_n,X,Z)\\bigr)\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\mathcal R_n(X,Z)=\\left(\\frac{3X-4X_{n-1}+X_{n-2}-2h f(t_n,X,Z)}{2h\\eta_d},\\ \\frac{g(t_n,X,Z)}{\\eta_a}\\right).\n$$\n\nUse $(2X_{n-1}-X_{n-2},Z_{n-1})$ as the Newton seed. Before calling Newton, if $(2X_{n-1}-X_{n-2},Z_{n-1})\\notin\\mathcal T_{t_n}$, return invalid-trial with the computed prefix. Otherwise call [[alg-finite-budget-newton-for-vector-residuals]] on $\\mathcal R_n$ with tolerance $1$, budget $B$, and $\\mathcal T_{t_n}$ as the evaluation domain. Append a candidate only when Newton reports root and the candidate lies in $\\mathcal T_{t_n}$; reevaluate $R_n$ once to record its unscaled residual blocks. Otherwise return the corresponding singular-Jacobian, invalid-trial, or iteration-budget-exhausted status with the computed prefix. The input functions are defined on the selected tube, so no separate evaluation-failure branch is needed. If all steps are accepted, return completed.\n\nFor an accepted step, the constant-step BDF2 derivative residual is\n$$\nr^d_n=\\frac{3X_n-4X_{n-1}+X_{n-2}}{2h}-f(t_n,X_n,Z_n),\n$$\nand the algebraic residual is $r^a_n=g(t_n,X_n,Z_n)$. The scaling ensures $\\|r^d_n\\|_2\\le\\eta_d$ and $\\|r^a_n\\|_2\\le\\eta_a$. The procedure makes no claim that Newton finds a root or that an accepted state is the exact selected branch root.\n\nEach step solves a coupled block system with $d+m$ unknowns. At most $B$ Newton corrections and $B+1$ Newton residual evaluations are made per attempted step, plus at most one residual reevaluation to record the unscaled blocks after a root status. Each correction uses one solve with the current $(d+m)$-dimensional block Jacobian. Work per residual, Jacobian assembly, and linear solve depends on the backend.",
